  "interpretation": "Fixed epsilon gives superpolynomial fanout on both ordinary sparse and maximally dense k-CNF scales. Choosing epsilon proportional to log(M)/n makes fanout polynomial, but the published O((k/epsilon)^(3k)n) clause guarantee, even with hidden constant one and capped by the original formula, certifies no fixed-power encoded shrink. This is a failure of this theorem transfer, not a lower bound on the actual sparsification output or on arbitrary SAT transformations.",
